Z||000000||Adrift||06-28-2001||07:46 PM||||How much would it cost me for a good paint job in the Toronto Area? When I get my fiero I will most likely want to get it repainted a high gloss black. Anyone have any comapnies they can refer me to? Anything I can do to make the process cheaper?<P>------------------<BR>My Dream Fiero, you ask?<BR>That would be a automatic '86 or newer V6 GT Fastback with T-Tops and A/C, fully running and for sale for under $1000 CAN. Know someone who's selling a car like this for this price in the Toronto area? PLEASE E-MAIL ME!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||06-28-2001||08:44 PM||||With paint jobs.  You get what you pay for.<BR>$500 will get paint put on your car<BR>$2000 will also get paint on your car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||06-28-2001||09:58 PM||||Prep work is the key.  Maaco can do a great job if the prep work is done right.  Not that I would take my car to Maaco.  The point is, prep work makes or breaks a paint job.  If you do it yourself you save a bundle and you know it will be done right.  A half decent paint job will run you upwards of $1500-2500 Canadian.<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||06-28-2001||10:00 PM||||As for the GT for under $1000...Yeah right!!!Although someone on the forum is selling a GT in Toronto for $500 without an engine.  Sounds like a steal.  It's ready for the engine of your choice.  Check in the Mall.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Huck||06-28-2001||11:08 PM||||I paid $2300 a month ago and got an amzaing paint job, with some body work... its worth the extra money to go to the best bodyman around.. it'll save you money in the long run if you plan on keeping your car for awhile.<P>Huck||||reg||1
